KIKUCHI MASAMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI KANETAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASHIMOTO, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSHINO, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIKUCHI, MASAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI, KANETAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A liquid crystal display panel in which a signal electrode provided on a first substrate (1), a counter electrode provided on a second substrate (2), and a liquid crystal layer (18) between the substrates joined with a predetermined space through a sealing part are arranged, and which carries out display by changing the degree of transmission and scattering by means of a voltage applied to a pixel part. A light source part (27) is provided along the periphery of both substrates, the part opposed to the light source part of the sealing part is translucent, and a polarized light separating device (30) is provided between the liquid crystal panel and the light source part (27).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un panneau d'affichage à cristaux liquides dans lequel sont arrangés une électrode indicatrice disposée sur un premier substrat (1), une contre-électrode disposée sur un deuxième substrat (2) et une couche de cristaux liquides (18) disposée entre les substrats assemblés, lesquels comportent un espace préétabli à travers une pièce d'étanchéité. L'affichage s'effectue par modification du degré d'émission et de diffusion obtenue par application d'une tension sur une pièce à pixels. Une source lumineuse (27) est disposé le long de la périphérie des deux substrats. La partie opposée à la source lumineuse de la pièce d'étanchéité est translucide, et un dispositif de séparation (30) de lumière polarisée est placé entre le panneau à cristaux liquides et la source lumineuse (27).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>